      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to find the measure of \\(\\angle CED\\), given that \\(\\angle BAE = 43^\\circ\\) and \\(AB\\) is the diameter of a circle with center \\(O\\), and \\(E\\) is a point on the circle. Let's go step by step through the reasoning process.\n\n1. **Identify Key Properties:**\n   - \\(AB\\) is the diameter of the circle, so \\(\\angle AEB = 90^\\circ\\) because it subtends the diameter.\n   - \\(E\\) is on the circle, so \\(OE\\) is perpendicular to \\(BE\\) (since the tangent at E is perpendicular to the radius \\(OE\\)).\n\n2. **Analyze Triangle \\(AEB\\):**\n   Since \\(\\angle AEB = 90^\\circ\\), we can find \\(\\angle BAE\\) by noting that \\(\\angle BAE + \\angle ABE = \\angle AEB = 90^\\circ\\).\n   - Given \\(\\angle BAE = 43^\\circ\\), then \\(\\angle ABE = 90^\\circ - 43^\\circ = 47^\\circ\\).\n\n3. **Use Properties of Tangents and Secants:**\n   - The tangent at \\(B\\) is perpendicular to \\(BO\\).\n   - The tangent at \\(E\\) is perpendicular to \\(OE\\).\n   - The line \\(AE\\) passes through the tangent point at \\(E\\).\n\n4. **Identify Relationships:**\n   - Since \\(OE\\) is the radius and \\(O\\) is the center, \\(OE\\) is perpendicular to \\(BE\\).\n   - \\(AB\\) and \\(BC\\) are tangents to the circle at \\(B\\), so these lines are perpendicular to the radii \\(OB\\) and \\(OB\\), respectively.\n   - \\(OD\\) is part of the angle \\(\\angle CED\\).\n\n5. **Determine \\(\\angle CED\\):**\n   - Since \\(\\angle CEB = 90^\\circ\\) (tangent at B), and \\(\\angle BAE = 43^\\circ\\), we need to consider the angles around point \\(E\\).\n   - The angle \\(\\angle CEB\\) and \\(\\angle ABE\\) both contribute to the total angle around point \\(E\\).\n\n   By symmetry and properties of the circle, \\(\\angle CED\\) can be found by considering the external angle to the tangents at \\(B\\) and \\(E\\).\n\n   - The angle \\(\\angle CED\\) is the supplementary angle (180°) to \\(\\angle BAE\\), because \\(AB\\) and \\(AE\\) are part of the larger angle sum of the circle.\n\nTherefore, \\(\\angle CED = 180^\\circ - \\angle BAE = 180^\\circ - 43^\\circ = 137^\\circ\\).\n\nThus, \\(\\boxed{137}\\).",
